 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: the entry Menelaus of p. 396 goes on here.",
  "col_left L2, L8: the commas after «II» are printed short (1.6 by 2.2 points, their feet 0.8 and 0.7 point below the baseline), like points at low resolution; read at 8,000 dpi, each is a head narrowing into a short stub, as the commas of the page, not round as its points.",
  "col_left L6: the comma after «n. 3» is printed short (1.6 by 2.4 points, its foot 0.85 point below the baseline). The lower left serif of the second X of «{sc:lxxiv}» stands apart from the letter, like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left L8: the two d's of «add.» are printed broken; read d.",
  "col_left L12, L16, L17, L18, L21: the e of «eius» (L12) is printed broken, open like c; the m of «gnorum» like rn; the first o of «nonnullis» open at the right, like ɔ; the o of «motus» and of «longitudinis» broken; several t's without the left part of their crossbar, like l («pertransit», «computantur»). They are read as the letters.",
  "col_left L14: «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i. The lower end of the first e of «emendata» stands apart from the letter, like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left L15: «*77*» is printed in italic figures, as the places of al-Battānī's text before «(adn.» in the lines above: both 7s overlap the italic 7s of the page by 0.84–0.86 of their ink (intersection over union), the upright 7s by 0.57–0.64 (glyph_iou.py).",
  "col_left L22, L23: the second c of «Occidentalis» is printed broken; the i and the c of «Ptolemaico» are printed touching, like k; the last o of «longitudo» is printed open. Read as the letters.",
  "col_left L29, L30, L42: «Sédillot» is printed with an acute over the e; «Čelebī» with the háček over the C and a bar over the last i. The i of «Mīram» in L30 has a bar (2.5 by 1.2 points); the i of «Miram» in L42 has a dot (1.4 by 1.0 points); each is transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L31, L41: «Mā-shā’-allāh» and «*mir’āh*» are printed with the sign ’ and bars over the a's.",
  "col_left L35: «*al-miǵlad*» is printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm; «π{sup:6}» is the Greek π with a superscript 6 (π⁶ Orionis).",
  "col_left L36, L37: «*miḥrāb*» has the dot under the h; «*al-mihraǵān*» has a plain h and ǵ.",
  "col_left L39: the Hebrew «מִמְסָךְ» is vowelled, read at 6,000 dpi: ḥireq under the first mem, šᵉwā under the second, qāmeṣ under the samekh, šᵉwā in the final kaf.",
  "col_left L44: «*283*» is printed in italic figures, though p. 283 of Part II is in Nallino's notes, which the index cites in upright figures (the same reference for α Canis minoris, p. 388, is upright): the 2, the 8 and the 3 overlap the italic figures of the page and of p. 396 by 0.73–0.87 of their ink, the upright ones by 0.42–0.61 (glyph_iou.py). Transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L45: «β» is Greek.",
  "col_right L1: «μῖξις» is Greek, read at 6,000 dpi: the circumflex over the ι is printed as a wave joined to the top of the ξ.",
  "col_right L2: «*mizāǵ*» is printed with ǵ. The comma after «II» is printed without its tail: a small teardrop (1.1 by 1.6 points, its foot 0.2 point below the baseline), narrower than the points of the page (round, about 1.7 points); read as the head of a comma, as the reference «II, {sc:xviii}-{sc:xix}» requires.",
  "col_right L7, L25: the V of «{sc:xv}» is printed broken; the guillemets around «Arabicus Propheta» are printed as small solid wedges, as on the earlier pages.",
  "col_right L10, L11, L14, L23, L24: several t's are printed without the left part of their crossbar, like l or ı («Battānī», «Mordtmann», «Moritz», «propheta», «legatio»); read t.",
  "col_right L15, L16: «Mouliéras» is printed with an acute over the e; «Mouravieff» with the ff ligature.",
  "col_right L18, L21, L23: «*al-mudīr*» has a bar over the i; «Mufliḥ» and «Muḥammad» have the ḥ sort; «*1*, *4*, *5*» and «*1*, *4*» (L24) are italic.",
  "col_right L19: the top of the italic f of «*Mufīd*» is printed apart from the letter, like a dot (1.3 by 1.6 points), before the bar of the ī (3.5 by 1.0 points); «*al-‘ulūm*» has the sign of ‘ayn and a bar over the u.",
  "col_right L27, L35: the first i of «al-Fārisī» and of «al-Khuwārizmī» is dotted, the last has its bar.",
  "col_right L32, L34, L37: the marks over the last i of «Ghāzī», «al-Ḥāzimī», «as-Sa‘īdī» (both i's) and «al-Mandā’ī» are bars (1.8–2.4 by 0.7–1.0 points), measured with word_marks.py.",
  "col_right L38: «aṣ-Ṣabbāgh» has the dots under the s and the S; the comma after «II» is printed thin (1.1 by 2.2 points, its foot 0.8 point below the baseline).",
  "col_right L40: «al-Akhṣāṣī» has the dots under both s, both times.",
  "col_right L41: the mark over the last i of «al-Aghzāwī» is a bar (1.8 by 1.1 points), though it looks like a dot at low resolution; «‘Alī» and «‘Omar» begin with the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_right L44: «Ḥaydar» has the dotted Ḥ.",
  "col_right L45: the mark over the i after the ‘ayn of «Ismā‘īl» is a short bar (1.6 by 0.8 points, as the short bar of an ī on p. 361); «at-Tanūkhī» has its bar.",
  "col_right L46: the h of «ash» is printed broken, like lı; «Maḥmūd» has the ḥ sort."
 ],
